pr_comments:
I think this PR is ready for review. It's currently based on https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/127277, so ignore everything with "DRA scheduler" in the commit message.

This includes the kubelet gRPC change. That one could get merged separately, but as it's also an alpha -> beta promotion, that and the API promotion should probably go in together or not at all. @SergeyKanzhelev, can you perhaps review "DRA kubelet: add v1beta1 gRPC API"?

@thockin: everything starting at "DRA API" falls into your domain. There's a workaround for https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/128448 in the last commit. That'll go away once there is a proper fix in master (should be soon).

I rebased to get rid of the commits which got merged through https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/127277 and of the "feature gate on by default" commits. The version skew testing from https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/127511#discussion_r1826989115 still applies.

I then looked at code coverage for [a KEP update](https://github.com/kubernetes/enhancements/pull/4948) and I wasn't satisfied with the low coverage of pkg/kubelet/cm/dra/plugin, so I added one commit ("DRA kubelet: increase plugin test coverage") to enhance that. @SergeyKanzhelev, @bart0sh, @klueska: whoever has time, can you review that?

@alculquicondor: can you approve for SIG Scheduling or do you want someone else to do that (@Huang-Wei perhaps)?

@towca, @MaciekPytel: are we good to go beta as far as SIG Autoscaling is concerned? I believe @towca has an implementation ready, we "just" need to get this and his https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/127904 merged.

@SergeyKanzhelev already [approved for SIG Node](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/127511#pullrequestreview-2414209829) and @thockin was [okay with the API changes](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/127511#pullrequestreview-2409136733) (nit was addressed since then).

This seems to cover it?

review_comments:
Linking @aojea and @pohly's out of band comments here to keep the conversation in one place:

@aojea: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/127511#issuecomment-2452650017
> I'm not much in favor of having this behavior by default on new clusters https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/commit/78d16b139b91e2d6a4991fae6f045f6f2d5875d5 , it will spam logs , retry connections ... that has an impact on performance and supportability on the platforms

@pohly: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/127511#issuecomment-2452661319
> Spamming the logs needs to be fixed. Checking for "is API group enabled" needs to be infrequent enough that it doesn't affect performance. If kubelet were to do this, it would be a clear no-go, but occasional pings from kube-controller-manager and kube-scheduler seem acceptable to me.

> Please consider this a proof-of-concept, not the final solution.
